WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.060
Welcome to Grade 2 English, Unit 4: The Big Sky.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:04.100
Look up!

3
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:10.940
In this unit you learn the words for everything
in the big sky: the sun, the moon, the stars,

4
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.800
the clouds and your own shadow.

5
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:18.720
You find out why a shadow is long in the morning
and short at midday, and why we have day and night.

6
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:25.260
You collect describing words for the sky and the
weather, you write true sky facts in the present simple,

7
00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:29.880
and you use verbs ending in -ed
to tell what you saw last night.

8
00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:37.800
Along the way you read “The Night Amal Counted the
Stars” and wonder about the world, just as Amal does.

9
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:43.740
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:51.220
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name
the things you can see in the sky: the sun, the moon,

11
00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.200
the stars and the clouds.

12
00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:59.940
You will also say what a shadow is and explain
how it forms when something blocks the light.

13
00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:05.940
You will also talk about how the sky changes
in the morning, at midday and in the evening.

14
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.840
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

15
00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:15.020
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: light, bright, high, sight, air, fire.

16
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.420
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

17
00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:28.160
The reading sequence includes A Poem: “My
Shadow” and Telling Time with a Shadow.

18
00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:34.260
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

19
00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.080
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

20
00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:43.060
The first language focus is Describing Words (Adjectives).

21
00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:46.120
An adjective is a describing word.

22
00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:50.580
It tells us more about a noun, which
is a person, a place or a thing.

23
00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:56.140
Adjectives help you paint a clear picture
of the sky, the sun and your own shadow.

24
00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.680
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

25
00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:05.000
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 — Describe the Sky.

26
00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.900
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

27
00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:14.190
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

28
00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.140
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:21.560
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

30
00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:28.160
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
